# NEON WAVE Multiplayer (Render)

## Deploy
This project is a Node.js WebSocket server that also serves `index.html`.

- Build command: `npm install`
- Start command: `npm start`
- Health check: `/healthz`

Push all files in this folder to the root of the GitHub repository on `main`, including `render.yaml`, then redeploy the Render Blueprint.

## Included in this build
- Public and private room creation, room-code joining, public room directory and online pilot names for users connected to rooms.
- No fixed member limit for standard rooms; 1v1 rooms cap at two players.
- Standard rooms broadcast an automatic start at 10 connected players; host can manually start at 3 or more. 1v1 manual start requires both players.
- Local coin wallet saved in the browser: +20 on each completed normal level, Time Trial rewards `floor(distance / 3)`, bot race completion gives no coins, each crash costs 2 coins.
- Revive at the crash point costs 10 coins when the player has remaining lives; restarting from the beginning is always available, even at zero lives.
- Shop: 3 lives for 50 coins or 5 lives for 80 coins. A valid daily redeem grants 5 lives, once per day. Invalid codes do not reveal the valid code.
- Harder obstacle timing and gaps, plus bots that steer toward upcoming gaps.

## Important limitations
- Coins, lives, name, and daily redeem status are stored in browser localStorage. They are not tied to an account and do not sync between devices.
- The public directory lists rooms and players currently connected to rooms; it is not a global account/presence service for people browsing the main menu.
- The client game still simulates each player's obstacles locally. The room server synchronizes player positions/progress and match-start events, but does not run a fully authoritative shared obstacle simulation.
- This package has not been deployed or tested in a live two-browser Render session from this workspace.


## Fixes in this build
- Added an on-screen ▲ UP press-and-hold control and independent pointer/keyboard holds; Space and ArrowUp both give an immediate upward boost and keep lifting while held.
- Entering the secret access phrase `TUK@TUK88` in the redeem box reveals the daily redeem code; it does not redeem lives by itself. Invalid phrases do not reveal the code.